<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

    <!--
        OpenTelemetry CPE-overmatch false positives.

        OWASP dependency-check matches the Java OpenTelemetry *definitions* libraries
        (semantic-conventions and protobuf-generated proto) against the broad CPE
        `cpe:2.3:a:opentelemetry:opentelemetry:<version>` purely because their version
        numbers fall inside the vulnerable ranges of UNRELATED OpenTelemetry components
        in OTHER languages (Go SDK, .NET SDK). These Java artifacts are pure data/codegen
        jars — no exporter, propagator, HTTP, or command-exec code — so they cannot carry
        any of these vulnerabilities. Different language, different codebase, different
        release cadence, zero relationship between the version numbers.

        All entries verified against NVD + GitHub Advisory DB (2026-06-15):

          CVE-2026-39883 — opentelemetry-go PATH-hijack via bare `kenv` (BSD/Solaris),
                           Go SDK 1.15.0–1.42.0, fixed in Go 1.43.0.
                           https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39883
          CVE-2026-39882 — opentelemetry-go OTLP HTTP exporters read the response body
                           into an unbounded buffer (CWE-789 DoS), Go SDK < 1.43.0.
                           https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39882
                           https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w8rr-5gcm-pp58
          CVE-2026-40894 — OpenTelemetry **.NET** (OpenTelemetry.Api /
                           .Extensions.Propagators) excessive allocation parsing
                           baggage/B3/Jaeger propagation headers (CVSS 5.3), fixed in
                           .NET 1.15.3. https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-40894
                           https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g94r-2vxg-569j

        Bumping the OTel BOM does NOT remediate these — the fixes live in the Go (1.43.0)
        and .NET (1.15.3) packages, not in the Java proto/semconv jars; any newer Java
        version would re-flag under the same broad CPE. Suppression is the correct action.
        First surfaced: workflow_dispatch run 26412295497 (2026-05-25); proto CVEs surfaced
        once Sonatype OSS Index + the full NVD scan ran on 2026-06-15.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CVE-2026-39883 (Go) and CVE-2026-39882 (Go) apply to opentelemetry-go,
            not to the Java opentelemetry-semconv definitions jar. CPE-overmatch FP.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.opentelemetry\.semconv/opentelemetry-semconv@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-39883</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-39882</cve>
    </suppress>

    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CVE-2026-39882 (opentelemetry-go OTLP HTTP exporters) and CVE-2026-40894
            (OpenTelemetry .NET propagators) apply to other-language OTel components,
            not to the Java opentelemetry-proto protobuf-definitions jar. CPE-overmatch FP.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.opentelemetry\.proto/opentelemetry-proto@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-39882</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-40894</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>
